# Shopify Files only for theme media

All storefront theme media — hero slider images, logo, favicon, banners, and videos — **must be uploaded to Shopify Files** via `uploadStoreAsset` / `uploadBufferToShopify` (`lib/shopify-files-server.ts`).

## Required

- Use `/api/admin/upload` with allowed folders (`hero`, `logo`, `favicon`, `logo-transparent`).
- Persist only Shopify CDN URLs (`cdn.shopify.com`, `shopifycdn.com`) in Supabase `store_settings`.
- Validate saved URLs with `assertShopifyFilesUrl` from `lib/store-media.ts`.

## Forbidden

- Supabase Storage buckets for theme assets.
- External URLs (Imgur, Cloudinary, raw GitHub, `/public/` static paths for admin-managed theme media).
- Saving arbitrary pasted image/video URLs without Shopify upload.

## Hero slider

- Each slide has separate desktop (1920×800) and mobile (600×480) images in Shopify Files.
- Hero folder also accepts `video/*` for future video slides — still via Shopify staged upload.
